l provenance was not retained (relation write failed: <msg>); the program's value is unaffected`) and consumes. This is the observable surface that works when indexing succeeded and the indexer (`index.cljc:549`, indexer state only, running before retention) has nothing to report. The Warning text is additive only — existing index/query contracts (`3\\\\nWarning: … materialize failed …`) still pass unmodified; no test contract was changed.\\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794405917000-engineer-cc3-fix-r8.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md:25:- `test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc` `repl-retention-failure-is-observable-test`: healthy defs first (handles present), then the store starts refusing only provenance writes; `(g)` still answers `42`, the Warning names the failed stage, exactly one admission-scoped failure with the right `:stage` is recorded, handles equal the earlier set (no incomplete handle, earlier survive), and an unclaimed literal round adds no failure and no Warning.\\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794405917000-engineer-cc3-fix-r8.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md:42:Note: one intermediate assertion (repeat `(g)` is unclaimed) failed on first run — each round mints a fresh admission, so a repeat call *is* claimed; the test now uses an unclaimed literal round instead. Contract change stated above: none to existing tests; the only new surface is the additive Warning line, `call-provenance-failures`, and `:call-provenance-failures` on session state.\\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794407164000-engineer-cc3-fix-r9.prompt.md:11:- Status-Event: 2026-11-12 09:5x +0700 | Model: muse-wonder-1.0 | Status: failed | Rationale: provider 429, quota window resets 2026-11-16T00:00Z (weekly boundary); zero work done\\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794390804000-engineer-cc3-fix-r5.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md:7:# cc3 fix round r5 — F2 caller threading, F6 maximum rule, bounded run v2: findings