{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc | sed -n '1,300p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yang.clojure.prelude\n     2\t  \"The `clj` runtime module (docs/design/yang.antlr.md section 8.10):\n     3\t   the published linker module every linked clojure program requires, as\n     4\t   `js`, `php` and `py` are for their frontends. It is written in prelude\n     5\t   notation and emitted with the same core machinery those preludes use;\n     6\t   it never runs on the host.\n     7\t\n     8\t   Three surfaces, mirroring the other runtimes:\n     9\t\n    10\t   - the entry, `clj/run-main`: initialize the runtime state, run the\n    11\t     unit — the thunk `yang.clojure/lower-unit` lowered — and answer the\n    12\t     program's value with the outcome model's `[:yin.k/ok value]`\n    13\t     wrapper removed, since that wrapper is frontend-internal. The\n    14\t     entry does not reset the global namespace: the namespace lives for\n    15\t     the task, so a projection the composition bound between two\n    16\t     entries and a definition an earlier unit published both survive\n    17\t     into the next unit's run (as `js/run-main` leaves `globalThis`\n    18\t     standing);\n    19\t   - the runtime global namespace, `clj/define-global!` and\n    20\t     `clj/global-get`: a task-local map in a cell (`clj.rt/globals`,\n    21\t     allocated once per task by `clj/init!`), keyed by export name. A\n    22\t     program's top-level definitions land here through its unit's own\n    23\t     publishing, and the conformance helper's export projection reads\n    24\t     and writes it — the one binding a linked unit reads a projected or\n    25\t     defined name through. A definition a unit runs publishes after\n    26\t     any projection of the same name and shadows it. The JS\n    27\t     `globalThis` table, the PHP named-function table and the Python\n    28\t     module dictionary are the same seam;\n    29\t   - the continuation family, `clj/try`, `clj/try-finally`, `clj/throw`,\n    30\t     `clj/raise` and its helpers: the\n    31\t     `%capture` handler-stack scheme the py/ts/php preludes carry, over a\n    32\t     dynamic-context cell `clj.rt/ctx` (allocated by `clj/init!`). It is\n    33\t     the reference implementation yang.clojure's exception lowering\n    34\t     converges onto (R3, section 8.10.7); the consumer wiring that calls\n    35\t     these entries lands after the family exists;\n    36\t   - admission, `admit`: the registry surface a linked clojure composition\n    37\t     needs beside the others — the `kind` module and the `portable`\n    38\t     adapters of the data exports the guest library's collection\n    39\t     predicates read.\n    40\t\n    41\t   The module pins the shared calling runtime (`yang.call`) at the\n    42\t   convention's call-address, as the other runtimes do, and refuses before\n    43\t   anything is published when a free name nothing supplies is read.\"\n    44\t  (:require [yang.core.prelude :as core]\n    45\t            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n    46\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n    47\t            [yin.vm.data :as data]\n    48\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n    49\t\n    50\t\n    51\t(def module-name\n    52\t  \"The linker module name of the clojure runtime.\"\n    53\t  'clj)\n    54\t\n    55\t\n    56\t(def runtime-keys\n    57\t  \"Every runtime key, each with an `:clj/uninit` placeholder at module\n    58\t   level so every read is discharged before `clj/init!` allocates the\n    59\t   real cell. They stay qualified: internal store keys, never guest\n    60\t   names.\"\n    61\t  '[clj.rt/state clj.rt/globals clj.rt/ctx])\n    62\t\n    63\t\n    64\t(def definitions\n    65\t  \"The module's definition list, in prelude notation (the module's own\n    66\t   `clj/` prefix is stripped on emit).\"\n    67\t  '[;; ------------------------------------------------- state and namespace\n    68\t    [clj/init!\n    69\t     (fn []\n    70\t       (if (= clj.rt/state :clj/uninit)\n    71\t         (do (yin/def (quote clj.rt/globals) (cell/new {}))\n    72\t             (yin/def (quote clj.rt/ctx) (cell/new (clj/ctx nil)))\n    73\t             (yin/def (quote clj.rt/state) :clj/ready))\n    74\t         :clj/ready))]\n    75\t    ;; the runtime global namespace: one task-local map in a cell, keyed by\n    76\t    ;; export name. `clj/define-global!` answers the value, so a publish\n    77\t    ;; sequence can chain through it.\n    78\t    [clj/define-global!\n    79\t     (fn [name value]\n    80\t       (do (cell/set! clj.rt/globals\n    81\t                      (assoc (cell/get clj.rt/globals) name value))\n    82\t           value))]\n    83\t    [clj/global-get\n    84\t     (fn [name]\n    85\t       (if (data/contains? (cell/get clj.rt/globals) name)\n    86\t         (get (cell/get clj.rt/globals) name)\n    87\t         :clj/unbound))]\n    88\t\n    89\t    ;; ------------------------------------------------------------- escapes\n    90\t    ;; The continuation family, mirroring py/ts/php (their preludes are the\n    91\t    ;; reference implementations): the dynamic context is one record in one\n    92\t    ;; cell, `clj.rt/ctx`, holding {:handlers} — clojure has no generators,\n    93\t    ;; no `with` managers and no recursion-limit hook, so there is no\n    94\t    ;; :depth/:base/:frame accounting the way py/php carry it. The handler\n    95\t    ;; stack is a chain of frames [tag payload rest n]: a :handler frame\n    96\t    ;; holds the continuation `throw` delivers to, a :finally frame a thunk\n    97\t    ;; of one argument (the thrown value, or nil) that every exit through\n    98\t    ;; it runs; n, the frame count, makes \"unwind to here\" an integer\n    99\t    ;; comparison. A first pass through a capture point is told from a\n   100\t    ;; re-entry by a flag cell, never by inspecting the continuation.\n   101\t    [clj/ctx (fn [hs] (assoc {} :handlers hs))]\n   102\t    [clj/rt-ctx\n   103\t     ;; the dynamic-context cell itself: `clj.rt/*` is an internal store key\n   104\t     ;; no closure of another module can name, so linked hooks read the cell\n   105\t     ;; through this export\n   106\t     (fn [] clj.rt/ctx)]\n   107\t    [clj/restore! (fn [saved] (cell/set! clj.rt/ctx saved))]\n   108\t    [clj/handlers (fn [] (get (cell/get clj.rt/ctx) :handlers))]\n   109\t    [clj/set-handlers!\n   110\t     (fn [hs] (cell/set! clj.rt/ctx (assoc (cell/get clj.rt/ctx) :handlers hs)))]\n   111\t    [clj/frame-depth (fn [hs] (if (nil? hs) 0 (get hs 3)))]\n   112\t    [clj/frame\n   113\t     (fn [tag payload rest]\n   114\t       (conj (conj (conj (conj [] tag) payload) rest)\n   115\t             (+ 1 (clj/frame-depth rest))))]\n   116\t    [clj/pop-frame\n   117\t     (fn [hs]\n   118\t       (cell/set! clj.rt/ctx (assoc (cell/get clj.rt/ctx) :handlers (get hs 2))))]\n   119\t    [clj/raise\n   120\t     ;; deliver `e` to the current handler stack; with no handler above it\n   121\t     ;; the value escapes the whole stack (unreached in practice: the entry\n   122\t     ;; installs a top-level handler). A :finally frame runs its thunk with\n   123\t     ;; `e` before the raise continues.\n   124\t     (fn [e]\n   125\t       (let [hs (clj/handlers)]\n   126\t         (if (nil? hs)\n   127\t           (:clj/no-handler e)\n   128\t           (if (= (get hs 0) :finally)\n   129\t             (do (clj/pop-frame hs) ((get hs 1) e) (clj/raise e))\n   130\t             ((get hs 1) e)))))]\n   131\t    [clj/throw\n   132\t     ;; the guest `(throw e)` form: clojure throws arbitrary values with no\n   133\t     ;; wrapping, so it is `clj/raise` under the guest name\n   134\t     (fn [e] (clj/raise e))]\n   135\t    [clj/try\n   136\t     (fn [body handler]\n   137\t       (let [saved (cell/get clj.rt/ctx)\n   138\t             flag (cell/new :first)]\n   139\t         ((fn [r]\n   140\t            (if (= (cell/get flag) :first)\n   141\t              (do (cell/set! flag :re-entered)\n   142\t                  (clj/set-handlers! (clj/frame :handler r (get saved :handlers)))\n   143\t                  (let [v (body)] (do (clj/restore! saved) v)))\n   144\t              (do (clj/restore! saved) (handler r))))\n   145\t          (%capture))))]\n   146\t    [clj/try-finally\n   147\t     ;; normal exit runs `fin` here; throw and escapes run it as they unwind\n   148\t     ;; through the :finally frame\n   149\t     (fn [body fin]\n   150\t       (let [saved (cell/get clj.rt/ctx)]\n   151\t         (do (clj/set-handlers! (clj/frame :finally fin (get saved :handlers)))\n   152\t             (let [v (body)]\n   153\t               (do (clj/restore! saved) (fin nil) v)))))]\n   154\t\n   155\t    ;; ------------------------------------------------------------- entry\n   156\t    ;; The outcome model's `[:yin.k/ok value]` wrapper is frontend-\n   157\t    ;; internal, so the entry removes one wrapper level from the\n   158\t    ;; program's value (a program returning that vector as data was\n   159\t    ;; wrapped again, so one level is exact). An error outcome passes\n   160\t    ;; through as the failure value for the caller to render.\n   161\t    [clj/unwrap-outcome\n   162\t     (fn [value]\n   163\t       (if (if (data/vector? value) (= (data/count value) 2) false)\n   164\t         (if (= (data/nth value 0) :yin.k/ok)\n   165\t           (data/nth value 1)\n   166\t           value)\n   167\t         value))]\n   168\t    ;; The global namespace is the task's, not the entry's: no reset\n   169\t    ;; here, so projections and earlier units' definitions survive.\n   170\t    [clj/run-main\n   171\t     (fn [body]\n   172\t       (do (clj/init!)\n   173\t           (clj/unwrap-outcome (body))))]])\n   174\t\n   175\t\n   176\t(def module-definitions\n   177\t  \"The module's definition list: an `:clj/uninit` placeholder for every\n   178\t   runtime key, then every definition, stripped.\"\n   179\t  (core/module-definitions \"clj\" :clj/uninit runtime-keys definitions))\n   180\t\n   181\t\n   182\t(def module-uast\n   183\t  \"The module tree: one wide application over the definitions, so every\n   184\t   sibling and runtime key read is discharged at module level. C1\n   185\t   finalized, like every production `yang.clojure` tree.\"\n   186\t  (yang/annotate-call-sites (core/module-tree module-definitions [])))\n   187\t\n   188\t\n   189\t(def module-exports\n   190\t  \"The module's exports: every `clj/` key of the definition list, stripped.\"\n   191\t  (core/exports \"clj\" definitions))\n   192\t\n   193\t\n   194\t(def ^:private module-free-names\n   195\t  \"The names the module tree reads and does not define, sorted: the host\n   196\t   exports its manifest must declare.\"\n   197\t  (core/free-name-vec module-uast))\n   198\t\n   199\t\n   200\t(defn module-spec\n   201\t  \"`yin.vm.linker.publish/publish-module!`'s spec for the module `clj` over\n   202\t   the host registry `registry`, pinned to the published `yang.call`\n   203\t   module at `call-address` — the convention's call-address, as every\n   204\t   runtime's publication carries. A free name nothing supplies is refused\n   205\t   before anything is published. This namespace emits; it never publishes.\"\n   206\t  [registry call-address]\n   207\t  (core/module-spec {:module-name module-name,\n   208\t                     :ast module-uast,\n   209\t                     :exports module-exports,\n   210\t                     :requires {'yang.call call-address},\n   211\t                     :free-names module-free-names,\n   212\t                     :skip? #(= \"yang.call\" (namespace %)),\n   213\t                     :registry registry,\n   214\t                     :message \"the clj module reads an undeclared name\",\n   215\t                     :refusal-ns \"yang.clojure\"}))\n   216\t\n   217\t\n   218\t(defn register-library-module\n   219\t  \"Return `registry` with host module `name` installed over `entries`\n   220\t   (`[export function]` pairs) at `arities`, each export pure.\"\n   221\t  [registry name entries arities]\n   222\t  (module/register-host-module\n   223\t    registry name\n   224\t    (into {} entries)\n   225\t    (into {} (map (fn [[op _]] [op (vm/primitive-profile op :pure (get arities op [1]) #{} :none)]))\n   226\t          entries)))\n   227\t\n   228\t\n   229\t(defn admit\n   230\t  \"Return `registry` with the guest library's host surface installed: the\n   231\t   `kind` module and the `portable` adapters of the data exports the\n   232\t   collection predicates read (yang.clojure's `library-adapters`). A\n   233\t   linked clojure composition registers them beside the other runtimes'\n   234\t   registry surfaces; a composition without a clojure program reads none\n   235\t   of them.\"\n   236\t  [registry]\n   237\t  (let [portable (into {}\n   238\t                       (map (fn [[source _]]\n   239\t                              (let [op (symbol (name source))]\n   240\t                                [op (yang/outcome-adapter data/refusal-message\n   241\t                                                          (get data/data-module op))])))\n   242\t                       yang/library-adapters)]\n   243\t    (-> registry\n   244\t        (register-library-module 'kind yang/kind-module yang/kind-arities)\n   245\t        (register-library-module\n   246\t          'portable portable\n   247\t          (into {} (map (fn [op] [op (:yin.k/arities (get data/data-profiles op))]))\n   248\t                (keys portable))))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
