50:            (let [[_ klass binding & handler] (first catches)]\n1060:                          (body-expression (map rewrite-throw-try handler)))))\n1088:  \"The raise of a call whose argument count no arity admits: it names the\n1173:(defn- call-entry\n1174:  \"The unary public entry, closed over a private argument-vector body. It\n1176:   escaping raise forwards an authenticated condition or wraps an ordinary\n1183:        raise (u/app (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v invocation) (u/lit :yang.call/raise))\n1199:        entry-body (u/app\n1207:                                    (assoc (u/app raise\n1213:        ;; (a raise from it propagates to the caller's own handler — the lane\n1215:        ;; vector [token args], selects it on the SAME unary entry. A guest\n1230:                 entry-body)\n1231:        entry (u/lam [invocation] packet)]\n1232:    (u/lam [body] entry)))\n1237:   a source form: entry-spelled source maps never pass through this constructor.\"\n1242:        ;; The factory closure captures the canonical descriptor and private\n1243:        ;; token. Projection reconstructs and compares that opaque closure;\n1255:  \"Publish a private body through a canonical constructor-created entry.\"\n1259:           (u/lit :yang.call/entry) (u/app (u/v 'dsg__make_entry) body-ast)\n1265:  \"Compile arities [{:params :body}] to one closure over an argument vector.\n1312:  \"A fresh closure over the convention that calls native `sym` with the\n1382:  \"Admit a source operator before common invocation. The raise exit delivers\n1386:   Only generated UAST implementation calls apply private closures directly.\"\n1394:          raise-exit (u/lam [condition]\n1395:                            (assoc (u/app (u/v 'clj/raise)\n1407:                             (u/lit []) raise-exit)\n1413:                          (assoc (u/app (u/v 'clj/raise)\n1418:          ;; A callee carrying a call entry is convention territory whether it\n1420:          ;; data-side invocation - a collection lookup or a raw closure call -\n1426:                            raise-exit)\n1430:                                (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'data/contains?) (u/v callee) (u/lit :yang.call/entry))\n1451:   serves a guest closure and an adapted native alike.\"\n1527:    ;; unit's public entry with the compiler's token packet (a two-element\n1528:    ;; vector: [token args]) - the private lane on the same unary entry,\n1958:  This is the main entry point that dispatches to specific compilers\n2003:          ;; a plain closure, never the convention's published descriptor.\n2134:          (reject! \"A :macros entry names a compiler form\" {:macros (vec hit)}))\n2205:   `[:yin.k/ok value]` on normal return and `[:yin.k/error raised]` on a\n2206:   raise. The `[:yin.k/ok|error]` wrapper is the harness contract (a linked\n2207:   entry's `clj/unwrap-outcome` removes one level); inside it, function\n2208:   bodies return plain values and a raise is the only error channel.\"\n2233:     ;; following definitions. Descriptor entry and body closures both capture\n2292:           ;; The two sibling closures share one frame: separate bindings would\n2293:           ;; retain one extra helper environment in every closure a guest\n2305:                                      ;; (yang.antlr.md 8.10.2), whose entry\n2318:                                      ;; branch and, entryless, is no more\n2324:                                      ;; carry no callable entry is not\n2359:                                                  dsg__entry\n2361:                                                            :yang.call/entry)]\n2362:                                              (data/callable? dsg__entry))\n2364:                                          (let [dsg__entry\n2366:                                                          :yang.call/entry)\n2370:                                            (if (data/callable? dsg__entry)\n2381:                               ;; The intra-unit dispatch